IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): section 2034 of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2034), "Assistance for
-- community food projects", lines 2981-3055 of usc07-ch51.txt (snap6's third range).
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the OLRC's USLM XML. It is not the official text, and
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- READING A RESULT: a MAYBE BOOLEAN answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, JUST TRUE where it says
-- yes, and NOTHING everywhere else ("not covered"). Every branch says which kind it is.
-- This section is addressed to the Secretary and to the entities that may get a grant; no household is mentioned.
-- The core has no Party for such an entity (NEEDS-CORE.md), so the entity's facts are inputs, not a party.

-- HELPERS (not a rule of the Act): three-valued AND / OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING input is passed through
-- unless another limb decides the answer without it (PLAN.md section 4).
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034 every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one limb is the text's no, so the whole is, wherever that no came from
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb says no
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: every limb holds

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034 at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: one limb holds
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every limb is the text's no

§ `s 2034 -- Assistance for community food projects`

-- TYPES this section needs (none is in the core).

-- (c): what kind of entity applies for a grant.
DECLARE `s 2034 kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 2034 a public food program service provider`
    `s 2034 a tribal organization`
    `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity`
    `s 2034 a gleaner`
    `s 2034 some other kind of entity`

-- (c)(1): the three fields of experience; the entity needs experience in at least one.
DECLARE `s 2034 experience` HAS
    `in community food work`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in job training and business development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in reducing food insecurity`              IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)(1): what a witness could say about a project.
DECLARE `s 2034 project` HAS
    `it is community-based`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it requires a 1-time contribution of Federal assistance to become self-sustaining` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed to meet the food needs of low-income individuals through food distribution, community outreach to assist in participation in Federally assisted nutrition programs, or improving access to food as part of a comprehensive service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed to increase the self-reliance of communities in providing for their food needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed to promote comprehensive responses to local food, food access, farm, and nutrition issues` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed to meet specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)(1)(B)(ii): the needs the text gives as examples.
DECLARE `s 2034 need` IS ONE OF
    `s 2034 equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project`
    `s 2034 planning for long-term solutions`
    `s 2034 the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers`
    `s 2034 some other need`

-- (d): the five kinds of project the Secretary shall prefer.
DECLARE `s 2034 preference facts` HAS
    `it develops linkages between 2 or more sectors of the food system`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it supports the development of entrepreneurial projects`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it develops innovative linkages between the for-profit and nonprofit food sectors`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it encourages long-term planning and multisystem, interagency approaches with multistakeholder collaborations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it develops new resources and strategies to help reduce and prevent food insecurity in the community` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (e)(2): how the non-Federal share is provided.
DECLARE `s 2034 non-Federal share` IS ONE OF
    `s 2034 a payment in cash`
    `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: facilities`
    `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: equipment`
    `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: services`
    `s 2034 some other contribution`

-- (e)(3): where the non-Federal share comes from.
DECLARE `s 2034 source of the non-Federal share` IS ONE OF
    `s 2034 State government`
    `s 2034 local government`
    `s 2034 private sources`
    `s 2034 some other source`

-- (g): what the Secretary may do for a community food project.
DECLARE `s 2034 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2034 provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development`
    `s 2034 provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects among government, private groups and the public`
    `s 2034 share information concerning community food projects with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties`

§§ `(a) Definitions`

-- (a)(1) "the term 'community food project' means a community-based project that (A) requires a 1-time contribution of
-- Federal assistance to become self-sustaining; and (B) is designed (i) (I) ... (II) ... and (III) ...; or (ii) to meet specific
-- State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs". A definition that says "means": a project that does not fit is not one.
-- src:2984 | (1) Community food project
-- src:2985 | In this section, the term “community food project” means a community-based project that—
-- src:2986 | (A) requires a 1-time contribution of Federal assistance to become self-sustaining; and
-- src:2987 | (B) is designed—
-- src:2988 | (i)
-- src:2989 | (I) to meet the food needs of low-income individuals through food distribution, community outreach to assist in participation in Federally assisted nutrition programs, or improving access to food as part of a comprehensive service;
-- src:2990 | (II) to increase the self-reliance of communities in providing for the food needs of the communities; and
-- src:2991 | (III) to promote comprehensive responses to local food, food access, farm, and nutrition issues; or
-- src:2992 | (ii) to meet specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs, including needs relating to—
-- src:2993 | (I) equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project;
-- src:2994 | (II) planning for long-term solutions; or
-- src:2995 | (III) the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers.
@ref s 2034(a)(1) Community food project (src:2984-2995)
GIVEN project IS A `s 2034 project`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` MEANS
    IF project's `it is community-based`
       AND project's `it requires a 1-time contribution of Federal assistance to become self-sustaining`
       AND (   (    project's `it is designed to meet the food needs of low-income individuals through food distribution, community outreach to assist in participation in Federally assisted nutrition programs, or improving access to food as part of a comprehensive service`
                AND project's `it is designed to increase the self-reliance of communities in providing for their food needs`
                AND project's `it is designed to promote comprehensive responses to local food, food access, farm, and nutrition issues`)
            OR project's `it is designed to meet specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the term 'community food project' means a community-based project that"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term 'community food project' means" (a definition that says "means")

-- (a)(1)(B)(ii)(I) to (III): the needs the text lists with "including needs relating to".
-- src:2992 | (ii) to meet specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs, including needs relating to—
-- src:2993 | (I) equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project;
-- src:2994 | (II) planning for long-term solutions; or
-- src:2995 | (III) the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers.
@ref s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs (src:2992-2995)
GIVEN need IS A `s 2034 need`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) the need is one the text lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER need
    WHEN `s 2034 equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(I) equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project"
    WHEN `s 2034 planning for long-term solutions` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(II) planning for long-term solutions"
    WHEN `s 2034 the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(III) the creation of innovative marketing activities"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including needs relating to" does not close the list

-- (a)(2) "The term 'gleaner' means an entity that (A) collects edible, surplus food that would be thrown away and distributes
-- the food to agencies or nonprofit organizations that feed the hungry; or (B) harvests for free distribution to the needy, or
-- for donation to agencies or nonprofit organizations for ultimate distribution to the needy, an agricultural crop that has been
-- donated by the owner of the crop."
-- src:2996 | (2) Gleaner
-- src:2997 | The term “gleaner” means an entity that—
-- src:2998 | (A) collects edible, surplus food that would be thrown away and distributes the food to agencies or nonprofit organizations that feed the hungry; or
-- src:2999 | (B) harvests for free distribution to the needy, or for donation to agencies or nonprofit organizations for ultimate distribution to the needy, an agricultural crop that has been donated by the owner of the crop.
@ref s 2034(a)(2) Gleaner (src:2996-2999)
GIVEN `it collects edible, surplus food that would be thrown away` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it distributes that food to agencies or nonprofit organizations that feed the hungry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it harvests an agricultural crop that has been donated by the owner of the crop` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it harvests it for free distribution to the needy, or for donation to agencies or nonprofit organizations for ultimate distribution to the needy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` MEANS
    IF (`it collects edible, surplus food that would be thrown away` AND `it distributes that food to agencies or nonprofit organizations that feed the hungry`)
       OR (`it harvests an agricultural crop that has been donated by the owner of the crop` AND `it harvests it for free distribution to the needy, or for donation to agencies or nonprofit organizations for ultimate distribution to the needy`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The term 'gleaner' means an entity that"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term 'gleaner' means" (a definition that says "means")

-- (a)(3) "the term 'hunger-free communities goal' means any of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd
-- Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992." The goals are in that resolution, which is not among the sources: asked as a fact.
-- src:3000 | (3) Hunger-free communities goal
-- src:3001 | The term “hunger-free communities goal” means any of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992.
@ref s 2034(a)(3) Hunger-free communities goal (src:3000-3001)
GIVEN `the goal is one of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(a)(3) the goal is a hunger-free communities goal` MEANS
    IF `the goal is one of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "means any of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term 'hunger-free communities goal' means" (a definition that says "means")

-- src:3000 | (3) Hunger-free communities goal
-- src:3001 | The term “hunger-free communities goal” means any of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992.
@ref s 2034(a)(3) the number of goals (src:3000-3001)
`s 2034(a)(3) the number of hunger-free communities goals` MEANS 14

§§ `(b) Authority to provide assistance`

-- (b)(1) "From amounts made available to carry out this chapter, the Secretary may make grants to assist eligible private
-- nonprofit entities to establish and carry out community food projects."
-- src:3003 | (1) In general
-- src:3004 | From amounts made available to carry out this chapter, the Secretary may make grants to assist eligible private nonprofit entities to establish and carry out community food projects.
@ref s 2034(b)(1) In general (src:3003-3004)
GIVEN `the entity is an eligible private nonprofit entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the project is a community food project` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(b)(1) the Secretary may make a grant to assist the entity with the project` MEANS
    IF `the entity is an eligible private nonprofit entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the project is a community food project` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the Secretary may make grants to assist eligible private nonprofit entities to establish and carry out community food projects"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to eligible private nonprofit entities for community food projects

-- (b)(2) "The total amount of funds provided as grants under this section may not exceed (A) $1,000,000 for fiscal year 1996;
-- (B) $5,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2014; (C) $9,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2015 through 2018; and
-- (D) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter." Fiscal years 1997 to 2007 are in no subparagraph.
-- src:3005 | (2) Limitation on grants
-- src:3006 | The total amount of funds provided as grants under this section may not exceed—
-- src:3007 | (A) $1,000,000 for fiscal year 1996;
-- src:3008 | (B) $5,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2014;
-- src:3009 | (C) $9,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2015 through 2018; and
-- src:3010 | (D) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter.
@ref s 2034(b)(2) Limitation on grants (src:3005-3010)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 1996 THEN JUST 1000000   -- (A) "$1,000,000 for fiscal year 1996"
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2008 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2014 THEN JUST 5000000   -- (B) "$5,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2014"
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2015 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2018 THEN JUST 9000000   -- (C) "$9,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2015 through 2018"
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2019 THEN JUST 5000000   -- (D) "$5,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): fiscal years before 1996 and 1997 to 2007 are in no subparagraph

-- src:3005 | (2) Limitation on grants
-- src:3006 | The total amount of funds provided as grants under this section may not exceed—
-- src:3007 | (A) $1,000,000 for fiscal year 1996;
-- src:3008 | (B) $5,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2014;
-- src:3009 | (C) $9,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2015 through 2018; and
-- src:3010 | (D) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter.
@ref s 2034(b)(2) Limitation on grants (the total against the limit) (src:3005-3010)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the funds provided as grants under this section, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` `fiscal year`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN
        IF `the total of the funds provided as grants under this section, in dollars` AT MOST limit
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may not exceed" is respected at or below the limit
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The total amount of funds provided as grants under this section may not exceed"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no limit is stated for that fiscal year

§§ `(c) Eligible entities`

-- (c) "To be eligible for a grant under subsection (b), a public food program service provider, a tribal organization, or a
-- private nonprofit entity, including gleaners, must (1) have experience in ... ; (2) demonstrate competency ...; (3) demonstrate a
-- willingness to share information ...; and (4) collaborate with 1 or more local partner organizations to achieve at least 1
-- hunger-free communities goal." The four are required together ("must ... and").
-- src:3011 | (c) Eligible entities
-- src:3012 | To be eligible for a grant under subsection (b), a public food program service provider, a tribal organization, or a private nonprofit entity, including gleaners, must—
-- src:3013 | (1) have experience in the area of—
-- src:3014 | (A) community food work, particularly concerning small and medium-sized farms, including the provision of food to people in low-income communities and the development of new markets in low-income communities for agricultural producers;
-- src:3015 | (B) job training and business development activities for food-related activities in low-income communities; or
-- src:3016 | (C) efforts to reduce food insecurity in the community, including food distribution, improving access to services, or coordinating services and programs;
-- src:3017 | (2) demonstrate competency to implement a project, provide fiscal accountability, collect data, and prepare reports and other necessary documentation;
-- src:3018 | (3) demonstrate a willingness to share information with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties; and
-- src:3019 | (4) collaborate with 1 or more local partner organizations to achieve at least 1 hunger-free communities goal.
@ref s 2034(c) Eligible entities (src:3011-3019)
GIVEN `what kind of entity it is` IS A `s 2034 kind of entity`
      `its experience` IS A `s 2034 experience`
      `it demonstrates competency to implement a project, provide fiscal accountability, collect data, and prepare reports and other necessary documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it demonstrates a willingness to share information with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of local partner organizations it collaborates with` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hunger-free communities goals it collaborates to achieve` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` MEANS
    IF `what kind of entity it is` EQUALS `s 2034 some other kind of entity`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (c) names a public food program service provider, a tribal organization, a private nonprofit entity and gleaners
    ELSE IF (   (`its experience`'s `in community food work` OR `its experience`'s `in job training and business development` OR `its experience`'s `in reducing food insecurity`)
            AND `it demonstrates competency to implement a project, provide fiscal accountability, collect data, and prepare reports and other necessary documentation`
            AND `it demonstrates a willingness to share information with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties`
            AND `the number of local partner organizations it collaborates with` AT LEAST 1
            AND `the number of hunger-free communities goals it collaborates to achieve` AT LEAST 1)
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "To be eligible for a grant under subsection (b), ... must (1) ... (2) ... (3) ... and (4)"
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible for a grant under subsection (b), ... must" (an "only if" in plain words: marginal reading (a); the other reading, (b), would answer NOTHING)

§§ `(d) Preference for certain projects`

-- (d) "In selecting community food projects to receive assistance under subsection (b), the Secretary shall give a preference to
-- projects designed to (1) ...; (2) ...; (3) ...; (4) ...; or (5) ... by (A) ...; (B) ...; or (C) ...".
-- src:3020 | (d) Preference for certain projects
-- src:3021 | In selecting community food projects to receive assistance under subsection (b), the Secretary shall give a preference to projects designed to—
-- src:3022 | (1) develop linkages between 2 or more sectors of the food system;
-- src:3023 | (2) support the development of entrepreneurial projects;
-- src:3024 | (3) develop innovative linkages between the for-profit and nonprofit food sectors;
-- src:3025 | (4) encourage long-term planning activities, and multisystem, interagency approaches with multistakeholder collaborations, that build the long-term capacity of communities to address the food and agricultural problems of the communities, such as food policy councils and food planning associations; or
-- src:3026 | (5) develop new resources and strategies to help reduce food insecurity in the community and prevent food insecurity in the future by—
-- src:3027 | (A) developing creative food resources;
-- src:3028 | (B) coordinating food services with park and recreation programs and other community-based outlets to reduce barriers to access; or
-- src:3029 | (C) creating nutrition education programs for at-risk populations to enhance food-purchasing and food-preparation skills and to heighten awareness of the connection between diet and health.
@ref s 2034(d) Preference for certain projects (src:3020-3029)
GIVEN `the project` IS A `s 2034 preference facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` MEANS
    IF `the project`'s `it develops linkages between 2 or more sectors of the food system`
       OR `the project`'s `it supports the development of entrepreneurial projects`
       OR `the project`'s `it develops innovative linkages between the for-profit and nonprofit food sectors`
       OR `the project`'s `it encourages long-term planning and multisystem, interagency approaches with multistakeholder collaborations`
       OR `the project`'s `it develops new resources and strategies to help reduce and prevent food insecurity in the community`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the Secretary shall give a preference to projects designed to (1) ... or (5)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the preference is for projects designed to do one of the five things

§§ `(e) Matching funds requirements`

-- (e)(1) "The Federal share of the cost of establishing or carrying out a community food project that receives assistance under
-- subsection (b) may not exceed 50 percent of the cost of the project during the term of the grant."
-- src:3031 | (1) Requirements
-- src:3032 | The Federal share of the cost of establishing or carrying out a community food project that receives assistance under subsection (b) may not exceed 50 percent of the cost of the project during the term of the grant.
@ref s 2034(e)(1) Requirements (src:3031-3032)
GIVEN `the cost of the project during the term of the grant, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the Federal share of that cost, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(e)(1) the Federal share is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the cost of the project during the term of the grant, in dollars` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no cost, no share to compare
    ELSE IF `the Federal share of that cost, in dollars` AT MOST 50% TIMES `the cost of the project during the term of the grant, in dollars`
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may not exceed 50 percent of the cost of the project" is respected
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not exceed 50 percent of the cost of the project during the term of the grant"

-- (e)(2) "the entity receiving the grant shall provide for the share through a payment in cash or in kind, fairly evaluated,
-- including facilities, equipment, or services."
-- src:3033 | (2) Calculation
-- src:3034 | In providing for the non-Federal share of the cost of carrying out a community food project, the entity receiving the grant shall provide for the share through a payment in cash or in kind, fairly evaluated, including facilities, equipment, or services.
@ref s 2034(e)(2) Calculation (src:3033-3034)
GIVEN contribution IS A `s 2034 non-Federal share`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` MEANS
    CONSIDER contribution
    WHEN `s 2034 a payment in cash` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "through a payment in cash or in kind"
    WHEN `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: facilities` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "in kind, fairly evaluated, including facilities"
    WHEN `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: equipment` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "including ... equipment"
    WHEN `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: services` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "including ... services"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including facilities, equipment, or services" does not close the list

-- (e)(3) "An entity may provide for the non-Federal share through State government, local government, or private sources."
-- src:3035 | (3) Sources
-- src:3036 | An entity may provide for the non-Federal share through State government, local government, or private sources.
@ref s 2034(e)(3) Sources (src:3035-3036)
GIVEN source IS A `s 2034 source of the non-Federal share`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(e)(3) the entity may provide the non-Federal share through this source` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `s 2034 State government` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "through State government"
    WHEN `s 2034 local government` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "local government"
    WHEN `s 2034 private sources` THEN JUST TRUE    -- TRUE-kind: "or private sources"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text does not say "only" or "nothing but"

§§ `(f) Term of grant`

-- (f)(1) "A community food project may be supported by only a single grant under subsection (b)."
-- src:3037 | (f) Term of grant
-- src:3038 | (1) Single grant
-- src:3039 | A community food project may be supported by only a single grant under subsection (b).
@ref s 2034(f)(1) Single grant (src:3037-3039)
GIVEN `the number of grants under subsection (b) already supporting the project` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(f)(1) the project may be supported by a grant under subsection (b)` MEANS
    IF `the number of grants under subsection (b) already supporting the project` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be supported by only a single grant under subsection (b)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "A community food project may be supported by only a single grant"

-- (f)(2) "The term of a grant under subsection (b) may not exceed 5 years."
-- src:3040 | (2) Term
-- src:3041 | The term of a grant under subsection (b) may not exceed 5 years.
@ref s 2034(f)(2) Term (src:3040-3041)
GIVEN `the term of the grant in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(f)(2) the term of the grant is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the term of the grant in years` AT MOST 5
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may not exceed 5 years" is respected
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term of a grant under subsection (b) may not exceed 5 years"

§§ `(g) Technical assistance and related information`

-- (g)(1) "the Secretary may provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development to an
-- entity seeking the assistance."
-- src:3042 | (g) Technical assistance and related information
-- src:3043 | (1) Technical assistance
-- src:3044 | In carrying out this section, the Secretary may provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development to an entity seeking the assistance.
@ref s 2034(g)(1) Technical assistance (src:3042-3044)
`s 2034(g)(1) the Secretary's permission to provide technical assistance` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2034 provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (g)(2)(A) "The Secretary may provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects and issues among and
-- between government, private for-profit and nonprofit groups, and the public through publications, conferences, and other
-- appropriate forums."
-- src:3045 | (2) Sharing information
-- src:3046 | (A) In general
-- src:3047 | The Secretary may provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects and issues among and between government, private for-profit and nonprofit groups, and the public through publications, conferences, and other appropriate forums.
@ref s 2034(g)(2)(A) In general (src:3045-3047)
`s 2034(g)(2)(A) the Secretary's permission to provide for the sharing of information` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2034 provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects among government, private groups and the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (g)(2)(B) "The Secretary may share information concerning community food projects with researchers, practitioners, and other
-- interested parties."
