    MAY `s 2034 share information concerning community food projects with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `(h) Reports to Congress`

-- (h) "Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to Congress a report that
-- describes each grant made under this section, including (1) a description of any activity funded; (2) the degree of success
-- ... in achieving hunger-free community goals; and (3) the degree of success in improving the long-term capacity of a community".
-- The deadline is a calendar date, so this is a function over dates (a regulative rule cannot carry it on the stable binary).
-- src:3050 | (h) Reports to Congress
-- src:3051 | Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to Congress a report that describes each grant made under this section, including—
@ref s 2034(h) Reports to Congress (the due date) (src:3050-3051)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2034(h) the date by which the report for the year is due` MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2014
    THEN JUST (Date 30 9 year)   -- "Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter"
    ELSE NOTHING                 -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text sets no report for a year before 2014

-- src:3050 | (h) Reports to Congress
-- src:3051 | Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to Congress a report that describes each grant made under this section, including—
@ref s 2034(h) Reports to Congress (was it on time) (src:3050-3051)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the date the Secretary submitted the report` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2034(h) the date by which the report for the year is due` year
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no report is due for that year
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the Secretary submitted the report`
        WHEN JUST submitted THEN
            IF submitted AT MOST due
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not later than September 30" is met
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF today GREATER THAN due
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter" (due date passed, nothing submitted)
            ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet due

-- (h)(1) to (3): what the report shall describe.
-- src:3052 | (1) a description of any activity funded;
-- src:3053 | (2) the degree of success of each activity funded in achieving hunger-free community goals; and
-- src:3054 | (3) the degree of success in improving the long-term capacity of a community to address food and agriculture problems related to hunger or access to healthy food.
@ref s 2034(h)(1) to (3) What the report describes (src:3052-3054)
GIVEN `it describes any activity funded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it describes the degree of success of each activity funded in achieving hunger-free community goals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it describes the degree of success in improving the long-term capacity of a community to address food and agriculture problems related to hunger or access to healthy food` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2034(h)(1) to (3) the report describes what it shall include` MEANS
    IF `it describes any activity funded` AND `it describes the degree of success of each activity funded in achieving hunger-free community goals` AND `it describes the degree of success in improving the long-term capacity of a community to address food and agriculture problems related to hunger or access to healthy food`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a report that describes each grant made under this section, including (1) ... (2) ... and (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including" states what the report shall contain but not what follows if one is missing
